{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Oh hey, you made it. I figured the parking garage swallowed you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Sorry.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): You're good. My sister was late to her own physical last month, same garage, and she would not stop texting me.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (DOCTOR): Come on in, have a seat. I'm Dr. Patel. How's the morning treating you?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (DOCTOR): Glad you got here. What brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Tired.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Tired. Umm, tell me how that shows up for you.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Constant.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Okay. Has it been days, or longer?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Months.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): When you take the stairs, what happens?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Breathless.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain with that?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): What about dizzy, or lightheaded?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): Have you fainted, or passed out?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (NURSE): Right. Vitals from a minute ago. Pressure was one eighteen over seventy four, pulse 92, oxygen 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Thanks. Uh, what's on her med list?",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (NURSE): Feros gluconate, three hundred milligrams, once a day.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): One fifty.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): One fifty milligrams, not three hundred. You still take it every day?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Alright, err, we'll leave that dose unsettled. How's the eating going, meat or mostly plants?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Vegetarian.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Strict, no meat and no fish?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Strict.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any odd cravings? Ice, or something else?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Ice.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Daily?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Daily.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): And your periods, how are those?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Normal.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any stomach trouble, nausea, or a change in your bowels?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): Have you had blood work for this tiredness before?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Borderline.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (DOCTOR): They said it was borderline. Do you remember which test?",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Hemoglobin.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (DOCTOR): No number then, just borderline. Let me look at your eyes real quick. Inner lids are a little pale. Lungs are clear.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (DOCTOR): What I'm thinking, only a working idea, is low iron. When iron runs low your blood carries less oxygen, so that's why you get so tired and breathless on the stairs, and the ice craving shows up with it. Being strict vegetarian can make iron harder to come by.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'm booking a blood count, a ferritin, and a B twelve. The lab will draw them today.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine.",
  "[SEG0048] person_3 (DOCTOR): Food wise, go for beans, lentils, tofu, and spinach, and pair them with vitamin C, oranges or bell peppers, so the iron absorbs better. Skip tea with the meal. Come back in two weeks and we'll go through the results."
 ],
